<<chatline "xX_FragQueen_Xx" "bro what are you LOOKING at 💀" "#e0556f">>
<<chatline "GhostReaper42" "IM JUST SAYING. the man has cheekbones. this stream is going to break the internet" "#e0b84d">>
<<chatline "TTVShadowMerc" "ethx if you're reading this please wear the pink thigh highs. for the culture" "#63b3ed">>
<<chatline "FragQueen" "i cannot believe yall are down horrendous for our streamer in a skirt" "#e0556f">>
<<chatline "GhostReaper42" "DOWN ASTRONOMICAL" "#e0b84d">>
</div>
</div>

The thread grows to two hundred messages in three hours. Memes spawn. Someone makes an EthX-chan emote for the server. It's a crude paint drawing of me with pigtails. Riley makes it an official server emote without asking me.

I scroll through it all. The energy is something I haven't felt from my community in months. Not pity, not obligation, not the polite engagement of people who watch out of habit. Genuine excitement, anticipation. They want to see this.

They want to see me in a skirt. The thought should make my stomach turn. Instead it makes something else happen. Something in the lower registers of my body that I'm going to ignore for now.

